cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ReadProof or ReadProof-Bench, please cite the paper below."
title: "ReadProof: an access-aware harness and benchmark for agentic search over social media"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jcaiagent7143-ui/readproof"
abstract: >-
  ReadProof is an open-source harness and benchmark that measure whether an AI agent actually reads the
  social-media post a user links (Douyin, Xiaohongshu/RedNote, Bilibili, YouTube, TikTok, Weibo, Toutiao, X,
  WeChat), under access rules enforced in code: declared identity, no cookies, no captcha solving or signature
  generation, robots.txt and Content-Signal evaluated on every request. It returns typed walls instead of page
  text, channel-located evidence (speech, on-screen text, captions, comments) and quotes verified in code.
  ReadProof-Bench v1 has Track A (145 posts, 522 link forms) and Track K (planted canaries).
